  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<h2>PWM Driver (Pwm)</h2><p class=\"lead\">Generates pulse-width-modulated signals with configurable duty cycle and period.</p>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<h3>Funktionen — Übersicht</h3>\n<ul class=\"mlist\">\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">void <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_00095\">Pwm_Init</a> (const <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_00111\">Pwm_ConfigType</a>* ConfigPtr);</code> <span class=\"dim\">Service for PWM initialization.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">void <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_00096\">Pwm_DeInit</a> (void);</code> <span class=\"dim\">Service for PWM De - Initialization.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">void <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_91000\">Pwm_SetDutyCycle</a> (<a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_00106\">Pwm_ChannelType</a> Channel Number, <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"platform.html#SWS_Platform_00014\">uint16</a> Duty Cycle);</code> <span class=\"dim\">Service sets the duty cycle of the PWM channel.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">void <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_91001\">Pwm_SetPeriodAndDuty</a> (<a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_00106\">Pwm_ChannelType</a> Channel Number, <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_00107\">Pwm_PeriodType</a> Period, <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"platform.html#SWS_Platform_00014\">uint16</a> Duty Cycle);</code> <span class=\"dim\">Service sets the period and the duty cycle of a PWM channel</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">void <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_91002\">Pwm_SetOutputToIdle</a> (<a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_00106\">Pwm_ChannelType</a> Channel Number);</code> <span class=\"dim\">Service sets the PWM output to the configured Idle state.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\"><a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_00108\">Pwm_OutputStateType</a> <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_00100\">Pwm_GetOutputState</a> (<a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_00106\">Pwm_ChannelType</a> Channel Number);</code> <span class=\"dim\">Service to read the internal state of the PWM out put signal.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">void <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_91003\">Pwm_DisableNotification</a> (<a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_00106\">Pwm_ChannelType</a> Channel Number);</code> <span class=\"dim\">Service to disable the PWM signal edge notification.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">void <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_91004\">Pwm_EnableNotification</a> (<a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_00106\">Pwm_ChannelType</a> Channel Number, Pwm_EdgeNotificationType Notification);</code> <span class=\"dim\">Service to enable the PWM signal edge notification according to notification pa rameter.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\"><a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"std.html#SWS_Std_00005\">Std_ReturnType</a> <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_00166\">Pwm_SetPowerState</a> (Pwm_PowerStateRequestResultType* Result);</code> <span class=\"dim\">This API configures the Pwm module so that it enters the already prepared power st ate, chosen between a predefined set of...</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\"><a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"std.html#SWS_Std_00005\">Std_ReturnType</a> <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_00177\">Pwm_GetCurrentPowerState</a> (<a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_00197\">Pwm_PowerStateType</a>* CurrentPowerState, Pwm_PowerStateRequestResultType* Result);</code> <span class=\"dim\">This API returns the current power state of the PWM HW unit.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\"><a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"std.html#SWS_Std_00005\">Std_ReturnType</a> <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_00180\">Pwm_GetTargetPowerState</a> (<a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_00197\">Pwm_PowerStateType</a>* TargetPowerState, Pwm_PowerStateRequestResultType* Result);</code> <span class=\"dim\">This API returns the Target power state of the PWM HW unit.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\"><a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"std.html#SWS_Std_00005\">Std_ReturnType</a> <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_00183\">Pwm_PreparePowerState</a> (<a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_00197\">Pwm_PowerStateType</a> PowerState, Pwm_PowerStateRequestResultType* Result);</code> <span class=\"dim\">This API starts the needed process to allow the PWM HW module to enter the requested power state.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">void <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_00103\">Pwm_GetVersionInfo</a> (<a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"std.html#SWS_Std_00015\">Std_VersionInfoType</a>* versioninfo);</code> <span class=\"dim\">Service returns the version information of this module.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">void <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_00189\">Pwm_Main_PowerTransitionManager</a> (void);</code> <span class=\"dim\">This API is cyclically called and supervises the power state transitions, checking for the readiness of the module and issuing...</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">void <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_00105\">Pwm_</a> (void);</code> <span class=\"dim\">The Pwm module shall call the function Pwm_ Notification_ accordingly to the last call of Pwm_ Enable Notification for channel.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">void <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_00198\">IoHwAb_Pwm_NotifyReadyForPower</a> (void);</code> <span class=\"dim\">The API shall be invoked by the PWM Driver when the requested power state preparation for mode is completed.</span></li>\n</ul>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<h3>Typen — Übersicht</h3>\n<ul class=\"mlist\">\n  <li><code class=\"sig\"><a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_00106\">Pwm_ChannelType</a></code> <span class=\"dim\">Nume ric identifier of a PWM channel.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\"><a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_00107\">Pwm_PeriodType</a></code> <span class=\"dim\">Definition of the period of a PWM channel.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">enum <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_00108\">Pwm_OutputStateType</a></code> <span class=\"dim\">Output state of a PWM channel.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\"><a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_00109\">Pwm_EdgeNotificationType</a></code> <span class=\"dim\">Definition of the type of edge notification of a PWM channel.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\"><a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_00110\">Pwm_ChannelClassType</a></code> <span class=\"dim\">Defines the class of a PWM channel</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">struct <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_00111\">Pwm_ConfigType</a></code> <span class=\"dim\">This is the type of data structure containing the initialization data for the PWM driver.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">enum <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_00165\">Pwm_PowerStateRequestResultType</a></code> <span class=\"dim\">Result of the requests related to power state transitions.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">enum <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Pwm_00197\">Pwm_PowerStateType</a></code> <span class=\"dim\">Power state currently active or set as target power state.</span></li>\n</ul>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
